/Title (The content and knowledge base of the chatbot itself isn't designed with much consideration to the user when the technology is applied in a real world setting, but the features that the user interacts with are certainly considered and accommodated for. The design and application of chatbot technology and broadly AI technology is evolving as the technology itself continues to develop. Chatbot technology is created for convenience, and it is continually improving to fit that requirement. Chatbots are more so designed with it trying to mirror human conversation, and while that is still a far goal, the improvements that are made to chatbot technology, such as more accurate intent recognition, make chatbot interaction closer to human interaction slowly and that provides convenience to the user. This technology is designed with the user in mind in that it is developed and built to mimic the users/humans. AI technology still stands to be a new technology and a dynamic field where the role the user plays or the application of the technology for user benefit is changing. Consideration of users in many different angles can help develop chatbot and AI technology, and more than what the users' role is currently, the future questions)
